From 25a661d0ee0daaecfd45a01b049c3addb3504d90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lance-index-build <lance-index-build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:25:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bench(index): equal-width controls for blocked vs per-vector
 assignment

The blocked-L2 ablation compared an AVX-512 4x4 tile with the 256-bit
per-vector batch kernel on AVX-512 hosts, so tiling and vector width were
confounded. Add:

- LANCE_SIMD_MAX_WIDTH=256: hide AVX-512 from runtime dispatch, so every
  dispatched kernel (tile, batch, pair) is at most 256-bit.
- LANCE_L2_BATCH_AVX512=1: opt-in 512-bit per-vector f32 L2 batch
  (l2_f32_avx512 per row); default dispatch is unchanged.
- Manifest records the selected f32 L2 batch and pair kernels.
- assign_micro: exact-assignment microbenchmark through
  compute_partitions_arrow_array on real BIGANN / GIST rows.
---
 rust/lance-core/src/utils/cpu.rs              |  53 ++++++-
 .../lance-index-bench/src/bin/assign_micro.rs | 133 ++++++++++++++++++
 rust/lance-index-bench/src/main.rs            |   2 +
 rust/lance-linalg/src/distance/l2.rs          |  84 +++++++++++
 4 files changed, 271 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
